From 29db2580bc26509b0ce8dd3f4225513b6ef67a8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:40:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 52/53] VC8-IP: on HT9050 + PCIE-1203 the ECAT-VC8 stations
 come from IO_Table.csv (IOType=Vacuum rows: InArm / OutArm / Index)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001: the vacuum modules moved -- InArm 0xA0, OutArm 0xA1, Index 0xA2 -- and they are to be set in
IO_Table.csv (a new IOType "Vacuum", Alias InArm / OutArm / Index) so the next change needs no code; only HT9050 +
1203 reads them. Rows in the table's own format, read through TIODATA like every other row (EastSun: "要照表照格式
照架構 轉成IP 160"):
    Vacuum,InArm,1,2,160,0,0,1,3,1,,,,     Lane = ring, IP = station (decimal), ISABase 3, Enable 1
Index2 / Index3 / Index4 name golden's other index modules (0x41 / 0x50 / 0x51) if more are fitted.

* database.cpp W906_ApplyVacuumStations(), LoadIoData's last step: only when general.ini Model=9050GPIB it fills
  VacuumUnit/Vc8Route.h's station table and moves every Sucker / Sucker_On / Sucker_Off row (ISABase 3, ring 1)
  on the module's golden station (0x20 / 0x30 / 0x40 / 0x41 / 0x50 / 0x51) to the new one, before InitSucker binds
  them -- so the engine's suckers, the IO page, SetIOTableByECAT_VC8_Sucker, the sucker gate and the Vacuum Unit
  page all use one station. An unusable row (unknown alias, ISABase not 3, Enable not 1, blank Lane, a hex / zero
  IP, a second row, two modules on one station) is skipped with a console line; golden's station stays.
* TMyVacuumPanel ctor: the panels' own numbers follow the same table (W906_Vc8StationMap).
* Not HT9050: nothing moves (golden). The ECAT-VC8 identity check still decides every read / write.
* tests/test_vacuum_vc8.cpp [12]: 147 / 147. IO-table ctests (MachineIoTable / IoPoints / MachineSuckers /
  IoWatch / InitDIOStstus / MachineCylinders / I115B_Vacuum) pass; production_audit unchanged.

